	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/audio_settings/help_strings">
		<string text="The sound and its devices, 3D audio, the volumes and voice chat."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Where the game's sound and the other players' voices play."/>
		<string text="Where the sounds around you come from. Headphones places each ahead, behind, above or below you, as the Xbox's 3D audio did; Speakers pans them left and right. Auto chooses by what you are listening on, and changes when you plug headphones in or take them out."/>
		<string text="Echoes sounds as the place you are in would, and muffles those behind walls, as the Xbox did. It costs a little of the processor."/>
		<string text="How sounds are converted to your speakers' rate. Clean is clear; Classic is brighter but harsher, and costs a little less."/>
		<string text="Turns all sound off or on, at once."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The volume of everything the game plays."/>
		<string text="The music's volume."/>
		<string text="Every other sound: weapons, vehicles, the world and the characters' speech."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Talk to the other players in network games: while Push to Talk is held (Key Bindings sets its key), whenever you speak, or never."/>
		<string text="The microphone voice chat listens to."/>
		<string text="How loud the other players' voices are."/>
	</strings>
